      "description": "Asset growth deciles: formation-period financial and return characteristics (time-series averages of yearly cross-sectional medians, 1968-2002).",
      "replication_meaning": "Demonstrates correct data ingestion and universe construction (NYSE/AMEX/NASDAQ nonfinancials, SIC 6000-6999 excluded, 2-year Compustat backfill filter, 1968 start), correct ASSETG signal construction (% change in Compustat total assets data item 6, nonzero-assets requirement), the Fama-French (1992) June-t accounting timing with December-(t-1) price for BM, and correct construction of every control variable (MV, BM, EP, Leverage, ROA, BHRET6, BHRET36, ACCRUALS, ISSUANCE, L2ASSETG). Matching the decile medians and the time-series-average-of-cross-sectional-medians convention validates the entire variable pipeline before any returns are computed.",
      "paper_quote": "At the end of June of each year $t$ over 1968 to 2002, stocks are allocated into deciles based on asset growth (ASSETG) ... The numbers in each cell are time-series averages of yearly cross-sectional medians, with the exception of average market value ($MV$-AVG), in millions of $, which is the time-series average of yearly cross-sectional mean capitalization. (L140)",
