      "table_ref": "Table II",
      "description": "Asset growth decile portfolio returns and three-factor alphas in event time (raw EW/VW returns, FF3 alphas by size group, four-factor robustness, decade subperiods).",
      "replication_meaning": "Demonstrates correct decile portfolio construction (annual June sort on ASSETG, July-t to June-(t+1) holding, yearly rebalance), correct EW and VW return aggregation, correct delisting-return treatment embedded in CRSP monthly returns, correct Fama-French three-factor alpha estimation, and correct NYSE 30th/70th size-group breakpoints. This is the paper's central result: it validates that the asset-growth-sorted portfolios produce the documented negative relation between growth and subsequent returns (Year-1 EW spread -1.73%/mo, VW -1.05%/mo) and the FF3 alpha spreads across all size groups.",
      "paper_quote": "Equal- and value-weighted portfolios are formed based on June($t$) asset growth decile cutoffs. The portfolios are held for 1 year, from July of year $t$ to June of year $t+1$, and then rebalanced. ... Panel C.1 reports three-factor alphas of the equal-weighted portfolios and Panel C.2 reports three-factor alphas of the value-weighted portfolios for all firms and for three size-sorted groups. (L401)",
