      "id": "T3",
      "table_ref": "Table III",
      "description": "Fama-MacBeth regressions of annual stock returns on asset growth and control variables (all firms and size groups; Models 1-7 with alternative growth variables).",
      "replication_meaning": "Demonstrates correct Fama-MacBeth cross-sectional regression methodology: geometrically compounded annual returns as the dependent variable, the base-model inclusion rule (nonmissing BM, MV, BHRET6, ASSETG; negative book equity excluded), time-series averaging of annual cross-sectional betas, and the first-order autocorrelation adjustment to the standard errors. Matching the ASSETG coefficient (-0.0922, t=-6.52 in Model 1) and its dominance over BM/MV/BHRET/BHRET36 and the alternative growth variables (5YSALESG, CI, NOA/A, ACCRUALS) validates the regression pipeline and confirms the paper's headline claim that asset growth is the strongest cross-sectional predictor.",
      "paper_quote": "To be included in any regression, firms must have nonmissing data for the following variables in our base model: BM equity, capitalization, 6-month lagged returns, and asset growth. We exclude all firms with negative book value in year $t-1$ ... The autocorrelation adjustment is made by adjusting the standard errors for first-order autocorrelation. (L1622, L1628)",
      "exercises_preprocessing_rules": [
        "fm_dependent_annual", "fm_inclusion_rule", "fm_autocorrelation_se", "fm_timeseries_average",
        "var_assetg", "var_bm", "var_mv", "var_bhret6", "var_bhret36", "var_l2assetg",
        "var_5yassetg", "var_5ysalesg", "var_ci", "var_noa", "var_accruals",
        "winsorize_assetg_robustness", "sort_size_groups"
      ],
